# Strategy & Execution Clinic

- Arabic is primary. All user-visible strings use next-intl. No hardcoded UI copy.
- Use CSS logical properties. Do not assume left/right.
- Light-first. Never introduce a dark-first shell. Use design tokens, never raw hex in components.
- Authorization is server-side via permissions. UI hiding is not security.
- Never trust client-supplied user id, role, hours, membership type as a grant, or credential status.
- Volunteer hours are append-only. No self-approval. Corrections are adjustments.
- Public verification uses an allowlisted DTO. No email, phone, or admin notes.
- Modular monolith: import other domains only through `modules/*/index.ts`.
- Do not implement payments, unrestricted AI, or microservices unless a later phase asks.
- Do not claim PASS without lint, typecheck, tests, and build evidence.
